{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-9-1","title":"Jeremiah 9:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Jeremiah laments the Jews for their manifold sins; 9 and for their judgment. 12 Disobedience is the cause of their bitter calamity. 17 He exhorts to mourn for their destruction; 23 and to trust not in themselves, but in God. 25 He threatens both Jews and Gentiles.</p>\n<p>O that. Heb. Who will give, etc. 4:19; 13:17; 14:17; Ps 119:136; Isa 16:9; 22:4; La 2:11,18,19 La 3:48,49; Eze 21:6,7 weep. Ps 42:3 the daughter. 6:26; 8:21,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-2","title":"Jeremiah 9:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>that I had. Ps 55:6-8; 120:5-7; Mic 7:1-7 for. 5:7,8; 23:10; Eze 22:10,11; Ho 4:2; 7:4; Jas 4:4 an assembly. 12:1,6; Ho 5:7; 6:7; Mic 7:2-5; Zep 3:4; Mal 2:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-3","title":"Jeremiah 9:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>they bend. 5,8; Ps 52:2-4; 64:3,4; 120:2-4; Isa 59:3-5,13-15; Mic 7:3-5 Ro 3:13 valiant. Mt 10:31-33; Mr 8:38; Ro 1:16; Php 1:28; Jude 1:3; Re 12:11 for they. 7:26; 2Ti 3:13 they know. 4:22; 22:16; 31:34; Jud 2:10; 1Sa 2:12; Ho 4:1-3; Joh 8:54,55; 17:3 Ro 1:28; 2Co 4:4-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-4","title":"Jeremiah 9:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>ye heed. 12:6; Ps 12:2,3; 55:11,12; Pr 26:24,25; Mic 7:5,6 Mt 10:17,21,34,35; Lu 21:16 neighbour. or, friend. every brother. Ge 27:35,36; 32:28; 1Th 4:6 walk. 6:28; Le 19:16; Ps 15:3; Pr 6:16,19; 10:18; 25:18; Eze 22:9 1Pe 2:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-5","title":"Jeremiah 9:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>they will. 5,8; Isa 59:13-15; Mic 6:12; Eph 4:25 deceive. or, mock. Job 11:3 taught. 3; Job 15:5; Ps 50:19; 64:3; 140:3; 1Ti 4:2 weary. Ge 19:11; Ps 7:14; Pr 4:16; Isa 5:18; 41:6,7; 44:12-14; 57:10 Eze 24:12; Mic 6:3; Hab 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-6","title":"Jeremiah 9:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>habitation. 11:19; 18:18; 20:10; Ps 120:2-6 refuse. 13:10; Job 21:14,15; Pr 1:24,29; Ho 4:6; Joh 3:19,20; Ro 1:28 1Co 15:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-7","title":"Jeremiah 9:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I will. 6:29,30; Isa 1:25; 48:10; Eze 22:18-22; 26:11,12; Zec 13:9; Mal 3:3 1Pe 1:7; 4:12 shall. 31:20; 2Ch 36:15; Ho 6:4,5; 11:8,9; Zec 1:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-8","title":"Jeremiah 9:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>tongue. 3,5; Ps 12:2; 57:4; 64:3,4,8; 120:3 one. 2Sa 3:27; 20:9,10; Ps 28:3; 55:21; Pr 26:24-26; Mt 26:48,49 in heart. Heb. in the midst of him. his wait. or, wait forhim.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-9","title":"Jeremiah 9:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>5:9,29; Isa 1:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-10","title":"Jeremiah 9:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the mountains. 4:19-26; 7:29; 8:18; 13:16,17; La 1:16; 2:11 habitations. or, pastures. because. 12:4,10; 14:6; 23:10; Joe 1:10-12 burned up. or, desolate. so. 2:6; Isa 49:19; Eze 14:15; 29:11; 33:28 both, etc. Heb. from the fowls even to, etc. 4:25; Ho 4:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-11","title":"Jeremiah 9:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Jerusalem. 26:18; 51:37; Ne 4:2; Ps 79:1; Isa 25:2; Mic 1:6; 3:12 a den. 10:22; Isa 13:22; 34:13; Re 18:2 the cities. 34:22; Isa 44:26; La 2:2,7,8 desolate. Heb. desolation. 25:11,18; La 3:47; Mic 6:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-12","title":"Jeremiah 9:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>the wise. De 32:29; Ps 107:43; Ho 14:9; Mt 24:15; Re 1:3 for. 5:19,20; 16:10-13; 22:8,9; De 29:22-28; 1Ki 9:8,9; Ps 107:34 Eze 14:23; 22:25-31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-13","title":"Jeremiah 9:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>22:9; De 31:16,17; 2Ch 7:19; Ezr 9:10; Ps 89:30; 119:53; Pr 28:4 Zep 3:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-14","title":"Jeremiah 9:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>walked. 3:17; 7:24; Ge 6:5; Ro 1:21-24; Eph 2:3; 4:17-19 imagination. or, stubbornness. which. 44:17; Zec 1:4,5; Ga 1:14; 1Pe 1:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-15","title":"Jeremiah 9:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>I will. 8:14; 23:15; 25:15; Ps 60:3; 69:21; 75:8; 80:5; Isa 2:17,22 La 3:15,19; Re 8:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-16","title":"Jeremiah 9:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>scatter. 13:24; Le 26:33; De 4:27; 28:25,36,64; 32:26; Ne 1:8; Ps 106:27 Eze 11:17; 12:15; 20:23; Zec 7:14; Jas 1:1 and I. 15:2-4; 24:10; 25:27; 29:17; 44:27; 49:36,37; Eze 5:2,12; 14:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-17","title":"Jeremiah 9:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>call. 2Ch 35:25; Job 3:8; Ec 12:5; Am 5:16,17; Mt 9:23; Mr 5:38 the mourning women.Those whose office it was to sing mournful dirges, and make public lamentations at funerals.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-18","title":"Jeremiah 9:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>take. 10,20 our eyes. 1; 6:26; 13:17; 14:17; Isa 22:4; La 1:2; 2:11,18; Lu 19:41</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-19","title":"Jeremiah 9:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>a voice. 4:31; Eze 7:16-18; Mic 1:8,9 we are. 2:14; 4:13,20,30; De 28:29; La 5:2; Mic 2:4 our. Le 18:25,28; 20:22; La 4:15; Mic 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-20","title":"Jeremiah 9:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>hear. Isa 3:16-4:1; 32:9-13; Lu 23:27-30 receive. Job 22:22 and teach. 17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-21","title":"Jeremiah 9:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>6:11; 15:7; 2Ch 36:17; Eze 9:5,6; 21:14,15; Am 6:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-22","title":"Jeremiah 9:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>fall. 7:33; 8:2; 16:4; 25:33; 2Ki 9:37; Ps 83:10; Isa 5:25; Zep 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-23","title":"Jeremiah 9:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>wise. Job 5:12-14; Ps 49:10-13,16-18; Ec 2:13-16,19; 9:11; Isa 5:21 Isa 10:12,13; Eze 28:2-9; Ro 1:22; 1Co 1:19-21,27-29; 3:18-20 Jas 3:14-16 neither. De 8:17; 1Sa 17:4-10,42; 1Ki 20:10,11; Ps 33:16,17; Isa 10:8 Isa 36:8,9; Eze 29:9; Da 3:15; 4:30,31,37; 5:18-23; Am 2:14-16 Ac 12:22,23 rich. Job 31:24,25; Ps 49:6-9; 52:6,7; 62:10; Pr 11:4; Eze 7:19; Zep 1:18 Mr 10:24; Lu 12:19,20; 1Ti 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-24","title":"Jeremiah 9:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>let him. 4:2; Ps 44:8; Isa 41:16; 45:25; Ro 5:11; *Gr: 1Co 1:31; 2Co 10:17; Ga 6:14; Php 3:3 knoweth. 31:33,34; Ps 91:14; Mt 11:27; Lu 10:22; Joh 17:3; 2Co 4:6; 1Jo 5:20 loving-kindness. Ex 34:5-7; Ps 36:5-7; 51:1; 145:7,8; 146:7-9; Ro 3:25,26 for. 1Sa 15:22; Ps 99:4; Isa 61:8; Mic 6:8; 7:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-25","title":"Jeremiah 9:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>that. Eze 28:10; 32:19-32; Am 3:2; Ro 2:8,9,25,26; Ga 5:2-6 punish. Heb. visit upon.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-9-26","title":"Jeremiah 9:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Egypt. 25:9-26; 27:3-7; 46:1-52:34; Isa 13:1-24:23; Eze 24:1-32:32 Am 1:1-2:16; Zep 1:1-2:15 Judah. Isa 19:24,25 in the utmost corners. Heb. cut off into corners; or, havingthe corners of their hair polled. Dr. Durell and others justly consider the marginal reading as far preferable; as being descriptive of the mode in which the Arabians cut their hair and beard. (See Notes on Le 21:5.)</p>\n<p>25:23; 49:32 uncircumcised in. 4:4; Le 26:41; De 30:6; Eze 44:7,9; Ac 7:51; Ro 2:28,29</p>"}]}